Torchlight: two passes with the same hash are grouped in the order they were made, not by
pointer. `PassGroupLess` (the map the opaque render queue groups renderables by pass in)
compared the passes' addresses when their hashes were equal - common, since many materials share
one RTSS program - and addresses differ from run to run (the heap's; Windows randomises it, and on
the console any change to what was allocated earlier moves it). The draws were the same, their
order not, and where two surfaces lie in one plane (a ground effect over the floor) which one
showed changed: the crowd fight's frame was 0.19% different between two pinned runs of one build
(2026-10-23). Each pass now takes a serial when it is made (`Pass::_getSerial`; `operator=` does
not copy it), and ties go by it. Not __SWITCH__-guarded: every target draws the same frames.

